---
/**
 * Plain text legal page — white canvas, no header/footer dividers (see
 * BaseLayout's `bordered` prop). Nav is the same hideHeader + inline <nav>
 * pattern as the Projects page (same padding/margins), not BaseLayout's
 * default bordered header.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { navItems } from '../../lib/nav'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How FES Agency collects, uses and protects personal data of users of this website."
  hideHeader
>
  <nav aria-label="Primary" class="relative z-10 bg-surface px-[var(--space-gutter)] pt-[var(--space-gutter)]">
    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-6">
      <a href="/" class="shrink-0">
        <img src="/fes-logo-dark.svg" alt="FES Agency" width="106" height="60" class="h-[var(--nav-logo-h)] w-auto" />
      </a>
      <ul class="hidden items-center lg:flex lg:gap-[var(--space-nav-gap)]">
        {
          navItems.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <a href={item.href} class="text-body text-ink-secondary hover:text-ink">
                {item.label}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <button
        type="button"
        aria-label="Open menu"
        aria-expanded="false"
        aria-controls="mobile-menu"
        class="inline-flex shrink-0 items-center rounded-[var(--radius-button)] bg-neutral-950/30 px-3.5 py-3 text-[1.0625rem] font-medium text-white backdrop-blur-lg lg:hidden"
        data-nav-toggle
      >
        Menu
      </button>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <section class="bg-surface px-[var(--space-gutter)] pt-10 pb-[var(--space-section-y)]">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-[760px] flex-col gap-10">
      <h1 class="text-h1 text-ink">Privacy Policy</h1>

      <div class="flex flex-col gap-10 text-body text-ink-secondary [&_a]:text-ink [&_a]:underline [&_a:hover]:text-ink-secondary">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <p>
            This Privacy Policy governs the processing of the personal data of users (hereinafter "User" or
            "Users"), collected in the context of the use of this website https://fesagency.pt/ (hereinafter
            "Website"), by Press Play, Unipessoal, Lda. (hereinafter "FES Agency").
          </p>
          <p>
            This Privacy Policy applies exclusively to the processing of personal data carried out by FES Agency in
            the context of the use of the website, in which personal information is deemed to relate to a natural
            person, of any nature and regardless of its support, identified or identifiable.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="text-h3 text-ink">Our Commitment</h2>
          <p>
            We ensure compliance with the obligations under Regulation (EU) 2016/679 of the European Parliament and
            of the Council, General Data Protection Regulation (hereinafter "GDPR"), and other legislation on
            personal data protection and privacy.
          </p>
          <p>
            The respect for your privacy, the protection of your personal data and the compliance with the legal
            obligations applicable in this area is a priority for us, which is why we are committed to only
            processing your personal data that is strictly necessary for us to provide you with the best service,
            ensuring respect for your privacy, transparency in information and the application of best practices in
            the field of security and protection of personal data.
          </p>
          <p>
            Where your personal data is processed by contractors, we will require them to provide the same level of
            security and privacy safeguards in respect of the protection of personal data.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="text-h3 text-ink">Data Controller</h2>
          <p>
            The Data Controller of the Users personal data is Press Play, Unipessoal, Lda., with the trade name FES
            Agency, with headquarters at Praça das Flores, 91, 4.º D, 4300-401 Porto, with a share capital of € 500,
            registered at the Commercial Registry Office under the sole registration and tax identification number
            513 906 169.
          </p>
          <p>
            FES Agency guarantees compliance with the regulations governing the protection of personal data by
            providing the following information regarding the processing of personal data of Users communicated or
            otherwise collected in the context of the use of this Website.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you need to contact us, you may do it via the following e-mail address: <a href="mailto:hello@fesagency.pt">hello@fesagency.pt</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="text-h3 text-ink">Purposes, lawfulness of the processing and storage period</h2>
          <p>
            The User can access, navigate, and use this website without necessarily having to provide any personal
            information, without prejudice to the navigation data necessary for the correct management of the
            website. However, the use of certain website tools may require the provision of personal data.
          </p>
          <p>
            In this context, the processing of your personal data has the following purposes, the basis of
            lawfulness and retention periods:
          </p>

          <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 pt-2">
            <h3 class="text-h4 text-ink">Website Management</h3>
            <p>
              The computer systems and software procedures used to operate this Website acquire, during their
              normal operation, some personal data whose transmission is implicit in the use of Internet
              communication protocols. This data (such as for example, domain names, IP addresses, operating system
              used, type of device and browser used for connection) is not accompanied by any additional personal
              information.
            </p>
            <p>
              The processing of this personal data is necessary to allow the use of the website, and that
              processing is based on the execution of a contract whose terms are governed by the Terms and
              conditions and, in the absence thereof, by the general principles of law. Your data will be stored in
              accordance with the information provided in the cookies policy.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 pt-2">
            <h3 class="text-h4 text-ink">Newsletters</h3>
            <p>
              The personal data provided by the user via the form are collected and processed for the periodic
              sending, by email, of newsletters and advertising material; and to receive updates on our activities
              and products. For the sake of complete information, we would like to point out that when sending out
              communications, FES Agency makes use of Mailchimp Platform.
            </p>
            <p>
              The processing of personal data is carried out based on your consent when you subscribe to our
              electronic communications. You may remove your consent at any time by opt-out available in the
              newsletters you receive by email, at which point FES Agency will no longer store your personal data
              for this purpose.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 pt-2">
            <h3 class="text-h4 text-ink">Contact and Complaints Management</h3>
            <p>
              The processing of this data is necessary for the reception, analysis, follow-up and response to
              requests for information and/or complaints. This processing is based on the legitimate interest of
              FES Agency in duly following up on your requests and in compliance with legal obligations.
            </p>
            <p>
              The data is only stored for the time strictly necessary to manage and fulfill the purposes for which
              it is collected, in compliance with the regulations in force and legal obligations.
            </p>
            <p>
              In any case, FES Agency adopts procedures that prevent the storage of data indefinitely and therefore
              limits the storage period in accordance with the principle of data minimization and storage
              limitation. Once the defined storage period has expired, we undertake to delete, destroy, or
              anonymize your personal data, except for the data that we are required by law to keep for a longer,
              legally determined period.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="text-h3 text-ink">Categories of Data</h2>
          <p>
            In the context of the mentioned purposes, we only process data that is strictly necessary for the
            pursuit of these purposes, namely:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6">
            <li>Personal identification and contact data (e.g., name, email); and/or</li>
            <li>Traffic data (via Cookies).</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            FES Agency does not process sensitive data categories revealing racial or ethnic origin, political
            opinions, religious or philosophical beliefs, or trade union membership, as well as the processing of
            genetic data, biometric data for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person, data concerning
            health or data concerning a natural person's sex life or sexual orientation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="text-h3 text-ink">Personal Data Sharing</h2>
          <p>
            The processing of the data collected is carried out by internal staff, identified for this purpose, and
            authorised to process the data in accordance with specific instructions given in compliance with
            current legislation.
          </p>
          <p>
            In certain cases, we may disclose your personal data, to the extent strictly necessary, to entities
            that provide services to us ("Processors") for the purposes mentioned above, under the terms of the
            contracts entered with them.
          </p>
          <p>
            In the event that your personal data is to be shared with service providers located outside the
            European Union, we will ensure that your personal data receives a high level of protection under
            applicable data protection legislation by arranging for the transfer under an adequacy decision of the
            European Commission or under the standard data protection clauses (or similar) approved by the European
            Commission.
          </p>
          <p>
            Your data may also be communicated to authorities or third parties when the transmission is carried out
            in order to comply with a legal and/or contractual obligation, a decision of the Comissão Nacional de
            Proteção de Dados ("CNPD") or another relevant supervisory entity, or a judicial order.
          </p>
          <p>In any case, personal data will never be disseminated, with other companies or brands for other commercial purposes.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="text-h3 text-ink">Rights of the data subject</h2>
          <p>
            In accordance with the law, and as the data subject of personal data, User may at any time request the
            right to access, rectification, erasure of your personal data, restriction of processing, portability,
            objection and not to be subject to automated decisions, depending on their applicability.
          </p>
          <p>In cases where the User has given consent for certain processing of your personal data, you may withdraw it at any time.</p>
          <p>
            To exercise any of these rights, you should do so by request to the following email address: <a href="mailto:hello@fesagency.pt">hello@fesagency.pt</a>
          </p>
          <p>
            You may also contact us on all matters relating to the processing of your data and the exercise of your
            rights under applicable law and, in particular, under this Privacy Policy, via the email address
            indicated.
          </p>
          <p>
            Without prejudice to any other administrative or judicial remedy, you may also lodge a complaint with
            the CNPD if you believe that the processing of your personal data by us violates the legal regime in
            force.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="text-h3 text-ink">Cookies</h2>
          <p>
            We recommend that the User read our <a href="/cookies-policy/">Cookies Policy</a>, which is an integral
            part of this policy, for more information on how we process your personal data through this
            functionality.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="text-h3 text-ink">Security Measures</h2>
          <p>
            We have a variety of information security measures implemented in line with national and international
            best practices to protect your personal data, including technological controls, administrative,
            technical, and physical measures and procedures that ensure the protection of your personal data,
            preventing misuse, unauthorised access to data, disclosure, loss, improper or inadvertent alteration or
            destruction.
          </p>
          <p>
            In terms of information security, we assume the same commitment to continuous improvement by which we
            are guided in our daily activities.
          </p>
          <p>Among others, we highlight the following measures:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6">
            <li>Restricted access to your personal data;</li>
            <li>Storage and transmission of your personal data safely;</li>
            <li>Protection of information systems through devices that prevent unauthorised access to your personal data;</li>
            <li>Implementation of mechanisms that guarantee the safeguarding of the integrity and quality of your personal data;</li>
            <li>Permanent monitoring of the information systems, with the objective of preventing, detecting and avoiding the improper use of your personal data;</li>
            <li>Protection of equipment for storage, processing, and communication of personal data, in order to avoid loss of availability.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            It is, however, the responsibility of the Users to guarantee and ensure that the devices and equipment
            used to access this Website are adequately protected against harmful software, computer viruses and
            worms.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="text-h3 text-ink">Hyperlinks</h2>
          <p>
            We may provide hyperlinks to other websites of interest, but we are not responsible for the privacy
            policy, cookie policy or terms of use of those websites.
          </p>
          <p>
            By accessing other websites through the hyperlinks provided, the operators of these websites may
            collect information about you that will be used by them. We highly recommend that when accessing other
            websites, Users consult all the information and conditions mentioned above.
          </p>
          <p>
            When you choose to follow us on social networks, when you interact with us on them, or when you access
            the site through them, your personal data may be processed by the organisations managing the social
            networks or the functionalities provided, in accordance with their respective privacy policies, which
            we recommend you to read.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="text-h3 text-ink">Updates to the Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p>This Privacy Policy may be revised and updated at any time and these changes will be duly announced on the website.</p>
          <p class="text-ink-muted">Date of last update: 19/02/2024</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
